IMPORT prelude

-- Countervailing and Anti-Dumping Duties Act 1996 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for an importer, a foreign exporter or a
-- Singapore producer caught up in a trade-remedy case: who is an "interested party" (s 2(1)); the dumping margin (s 2(1), s 14(1));
-- the amount of duty (ss 3(2), 14(2)); standing to petition (ss 4(8), 19(8)); the sufficiency of home-market sales (s 15(3));
-- termination for a de minimis margin or negligible volume (s 24(2), (3)); the length of an investigation (ss 6, 20); when
-- provisional measures may start and how long they last (ss 8(2), (4), 22(2)); what happens to provisional duty at the end
-- (ss 9(5)-(7), 23(5)-(7)); retroactive duty (ss 9(8), 23(8)); the five-year sunset (ss 12(7), 26(7)); review by the Tribunal
-- (ss 13, 27); double counting (s 42); currency movements (s 33(5)); and the secrecy offence (s 45).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021"), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CADDA1996.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026 as the current
-- version). The latest amending Act annotated in the text is [21/2008] (s 30(5)); the legislative history lists Act 21 of 2008
-- (Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008, in force 1 March 2010) as the last amendment.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0098 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the rules with a figure, a deadline or a yes/no an affected business can test. Not encoded:
-- the definition of a countervailable subsidy (s 2(2)-(5)), normal value and export price construction beyond the 5% test
-- (ss 15(1), (2), (4)-(7), 16-18), the Minister's procedural duties to publish and notify (ss 4(3)-(7), 7, 9(3), 21, 23(3)),
-- undertakings (ss 11, 25) beyond the 120-day deadline, the review grounds (ss 12(1), 26(1)), Part 4 administration, the Tribunal's
-- constitution (s 30), confidential information (s 35), facts available (s 37), and every rule left to regulations (none were
-- retrieved). Anything turning on the Minister's judgment (injury, causation, public interest, "special circumstances") is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Countervailing and Anti-Dumping Duties Act 1996 -- duties`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2(1) -- interested party`

-- s 2(1): "interested party" means (a) "a producer, an exporter or an importer of the subject goods"; (b) a trade or business
-- association a majority of whose members are producers, exporters or importers of the subject goods; (c) the government of the
-- producing or exporting country; (d) "a producer of the like goods in Singapore"; (e) an association a majority of whose members
-- produce the like goods in Singapore; or (f) "any other person the Minister considers appropriate".
-- A retailer or industrial user who buys the goods after import, and a consumer, fall only under (f).
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `an importer of the subject goods`
    `a foreign exporter of the subject goods`
    `a foreign producer of the subject goods`
    `a Singapore producer of like goods`
    `an association mostly of importers of the subject goods`
    `an association mostly of Singapore producers of like goods`
    `the government of the exporting country`
    `a Singapore manufacturer using the goods as an input`
    `a consumer association`
    `a retail buyer`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the Minister considers the person appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an interested party` IF
        `the Minister considers the person appropriate`
    OR  CONSIDER `the person`
        WHEN `a Singapore manufacturer using the goods as an input` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a consumer association` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a retail buyer` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(1), 14(1)(a), 14(2), 3(2) -- dumping margin and the amount of duty`

-- s 2(1): "dumping margin" means "the amount by which the normal value of the subject goods exceeds the export price".
-- s 14(1)(a): duty may be imposed where "the export price of the subject goods is less than the normal value" (and injury, (b)).
-- s 14(2) (s 3(2) for subsidies, in the same words): the duty "(a) is equal to the dumping margin ...; or (b) if the Minister
-- determines that a lower anti-dumping duty will be sufficient to eliminate the injury ..., is such lower duty".
GIVEN `normal value` IS A NUMBER, `export price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dumping margin` MEANS
    IF `normal value` GREATER THAN `export price` THEN `normal value` MINUS `export price` ELSE 0

GIVEN `normal value` IS A NUMBER, `export price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are dumped` IF
    `export price` LESS THAN `normal value`

GIVEN `margin or subsidy` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister found a lower duty sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN, `the lower duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the duty to be imposed` MEANS
    IF `the Minister found a lower duty sufficient` AND `the lower duty` LESS THAN `margin or subsidy`
    THEN `the lower duty`
    ELSE `margin or subsidy`

§§ `4(8), 19(8) -- standing of the petition`

-- s 19(8) (s 4(8) in the same words): the Minister "must not initiate an investigation" unless (a) the petition "is supported by
-- domestic producers of like goods whose collective output constitutes more than 50% of the total production of the like goods
-- produced by that portion of the domestic industry expressing either support for or opposition to the written petition"; and
-- (b) the producers "expressly supporting the written petition account for at least 25% of the total production of the like goods
-- produced by the domestic industry". Producers who say nothing count only in (b).
GIVEN `output supporting` IS A NUMBER, `output opposing` IS A NUMBER, `total domestic output` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the petition has enough support to initiate` IF
        `output supporting` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `output supporting` PLUS `output opposing`
    AND `output supporting` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `total domestic output`

§§ `15(3) -- enough home-market sales to set normal value`

-- s 15(3): home-market (or third-country) sales are "normally considered a sufficient quantity ... if such sales constitute 5% or
-- more of the sales of the subject goods to Singapore, except that a lower ratio is acceptable where the evidence shows that
-- domestic sales at such lower ratio are of sufficient magnitude to provide for a proper comparison".
GIVEN `home-market sales` IS A NUMBER, `sales to Singapore` IS A NUMBER, `evidence shows a lower ratio suffices` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `home-market sales are sufficient` IF
        `home-market sales` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `sales to Singapore` TIMES 5
    OR  `evidence shows a lower ratio suffices`

§§ `24(2), (3) -- de minimis margin and negligible volume`

-- s 24(2): an anti-dumping investigation "must be terminated immediately" if the margin is de minimis or the volume "or the injury,
-- is negligible". (3)(a): de minimis means "less than 2%, expressed as a percentage of the export price"; (b): volume is "normally"
-- negligible if the country accounts "for less than 3% of imports of the like goods into Singapore, unless the subject goods from
-- countries which individually account for less than 3% ... collectively account for more than 7%".
-- For countervailing duty, s 10(3) leaves both thresholds to "the prescribed percentage": the Act states no figure.
GIVEN `normal value` IS A NUMBER, `export price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dumping margin is de minimis` IF
    (`the dumping margin` `normal value` `export price`) TIMES 100 LESS THAN `export price` TIMES 2

GIVEN `country share in percent` IS A NUMBER, `combined share of all sub-3% countries in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the volume is negligible` IF
        `country share in percent` LESS THAN 3
    AND `combined share of all sub-3% countries in percent` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `normal value` IS A NUMBER, `export price` IS A NUMBER, `country share in percent` IS A NUMBER,
      `combined share of all sub-3% countries in percent` IS A NUMBER, `the injury is negligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the anti-dumping investigation must be terminated` IF
        `the dumping margin is de minimis` `normal value` `export price`
    OR  `the volume is negligible` `country share in percent` `combined share of all sub-3% countries in percent`
    OR  `the injury is negligible`

§§ `6, 20 -- length of an investigation`

-- s 20 (s 6 in the same words): investigations "must, except in special circumstances, be concluded by the Minister within one year,
-- and in no case more than 18 months after initiation".
GIVEN `months since initiation` IS A NUMBER, `special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the investigation may still be concluded` IF
        `months since initiation` AT MOST 12
    OR  (`special circumstances` AND `months since initiation` AT MOST 18)

§§ `8(2), (4), 22(2), (4) -- provisional measures`

-- s 22(2) (s 8(2) the same): provisional measures "must not be imposed sooner than 60 days from the date of initiation".
-- s 8(4) (countervailing): limited "to as short a period as possible but must in no case exceed 4 months".
-- s 22(4) (anti-dumping): "must not exceed such period as may be prescribed" -- the Act states no figure.
DECLARE Remedy IS ONE OF
    `anti-dumping duty`
    `countervailing duty`

GIVEN `days after initiation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `provisional measures may begin` IF
    `days after initiation` AT LEAST 60

GIVEN `the remedy` IS A Remedy, `months applied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act itself caps the provisional period and it is exceeded` IF
    CONSIDER `the remedy`
    WHEN `countervailing duty` THEN `months applied` GREATER THAN 4
    WHEN `anti-dumping duty` THEN FALSE

§§ `9(5)-(7), 23(5)-(7) -- provisional duty at the final determination`

-- s 23(5) (s 9(5) the same): duty is imposed on goods that bore provisional measures only if the Minister finds (a) "material
-- injury", or (b) "threat of material injury" and that, without the provisional measures, the imports "would have led to a finding of
-- material injury". A finding of material retardation alone is not listed.
-- s 23(6): where the final duty "is higher than the provisional duty or the amount guaranteed by the security ..., only the amount
-- equal to the provisional duty or the security given is to be imposed"; where it "is less", the full final duty is imposed and "the
-- excess ... must be reimbursed or released". (7): where no duty is imposed under (5), the provisional duty is refunded and the
-- security released.
DECLARE Injury IS ONE OF
    `material injury`
    `threat of material injury`
    `material retardation of an industry`
    `no injury`

GIVEN `the finding` IS A Injury, `would have been material injury without the provisional measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `duty is imposed on provisionally covered goods` IF
    CONSIDER `the finding`
    WHEN `material injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `threat of material injury` THEN `would have been material injury without the provisional measures`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the finding` IS A Injury, `would have been material injury without the provisional measures` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `final duty` IS A NUMBER, `provisional amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount kept on provisionally covered goods` MEANS
    IF `duty is imposed on provisionally covered goods` `the finding` `would have been material injury without the provisional measures`
    THEN `the lesser of` `final duty` `provisional amount`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the finding` IS A Injury, `would have been material injury without the provisional measures` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `final duty` IS A NUMBER, `provisional amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount refunded or released` MEANS
    `provisional amount` MINUS `the amount kept on provisionally covered goods` `the finding` `would have been material injury without the provisional measures` `final duty` `provisional amount`

§§ `9(8), 23(8) -- retroactive duty`

-- s 23(8): anti-dumping duty may reach goods imported "within a period of 90 days prior to the application of provisional measures,
-- but in no case earlier than the date of the initiation of the investigation, if (a) there is a history of dumping which caused
-- injury, or the importer was or should have been aware that the exporter practises dumping and that such dumping would cause
-- injury; and (b) the injury is caused by massive dumped imports ... in a relatively short period".
-- s 9(8) (countervailing): (a) "injury that is difficult to repair"; (b) massive imports in a relatively short period and
-- retroactive duty "necessary to preclude the recurrence"; and (c) subsidies inconsistent with GATT 1994 and the Subsidies Agreement.
-- Days are counted from initiation; the provisional measures began on `provisional day`.
GIVEN `history of injurious dumping` IS A BOOLEAN, `importer knew or should have known` IS A BOOLEAN, `massive imports undermining the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the anti-dumping conditions for retroactive duty are met` IF
    (`history of injurious dumping` OR `importer knew or should have known`) AND `massive imports undermining the duty`

GIVEN `difficult to repair` IS A BOOLEAN, `massive imports and retroactivity necessary` IS A BOOLEAN, `subsidies inconsistent with WTO rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the countervailing conditions for retroactive duty are met` IF
    `difficult to repair` AND `massive imports and retroactivity necessary` AND `subsidies inconsistent with WTO rules`

GIVEN `import day` IS A NUMBER, `provisional day` IS A NUMBER, `conditions met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the import may bear retroactive duty` IF
        `conditions met`
    AND `import day` LESS THAN `provisional day`
    AND `import day` AT LEAST `provisional day` MINUS 90
    AND `import day` AT LEAST 0

§§ `12(7), 26(7) -- five-year sunset`

-- s 26(7) (s 12(7) the same): duties "must not be collected on imports made after 5 years from the date of publication of the notice
-- of the final determination", and undertakings lapse likewise, "unless the Minister determines on the basis of a review ... that
-- the termination ... would be likely to lead to continuation or recurrence" of dumping (or subsidisation) and injury.
GIVEN `years after publication` IS A NUMBER, `a review found recurrence likely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `duty may be collected on the import` IF
        `years after publication` AT MOST 5
    OR  `a review found recurrence likely`

§§ `13, 27 -- review by the Tribunal`

-- s 27(1) (s 13(1) the same): "An interested party has the right of review by the Tribunal" against a final determination or a final
-- determination in a review. (2): "must be filed within 30 days" of the notice. (3): the Tribunal may "affirm the determination or
-- remit the matter to the Minister for reconsideration". s 30(8): it asks "whether there is substantial evidence on the record to
-- support the Minister's decision".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the Minister considers the person appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to the Tribunal` IF
        `is an interested party` `the person` `the Minister considers the person appropriate`
    AND `days since notice` AT MOST 30

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `affirm the determination`
    `remit to the Minister for reconsideration`
    `substitute its own duty rate`
    `annul the duty`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may order` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `affirm the determination` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `remit to the Minister for reconsideration` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `25(9)(c) -- resumed investigation after an undertaking is broken`

-- s 25(9)(c): on resuming an anti-dumping investigation the Minister makes a final determination "within 120 days after the
-- publication of the preliminary determination". s 11(9)(c) (countervailing) says "within the prescribed period" instead.
GIVEN `days after preliminary determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resumed anti-dumping final determination is in time` IF
    `days after preliminary determination` AT MOST 120

§§ `33(5), 42 -- exchange rates and double counting`

-- s 33(5): where the Minister is satisfied an exchange rate "has undergone a sustained movement during the period of investigation,
-- the Minister must allow exporters at least 60 days to adjust their export prices".
-- s 42: "No goods may be subject to both anti-dumping and countervailing duties to compensate for the same situation of dumping and
-- export subsidisation."
GIVEN `sustained movement` IS A BOOLEAN, `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exporter was given enough time to adjust` IF
    (NOT `sustained movement`) OR `days allowed` AT LEAST 60

GIVEN `same situation of dumping and export subsidisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `both duties may be imposed` IF
    NOT `same situation of dumping and export subsidisation`

§§ `45 -- obligation of secrecy`

-- s 45(1): no person with access to material "obtained pursuant to the provisions of this Act" may disclose it "unless such
-- disclosure is (a) authorised by the Minister; or (b) made for the purposes of this Act". (2): "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or ... both".
GIVEN `disclosed the material` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
    `disclosed the material` AND (NOT `authorised by the Minister`) AND (NOT `for the purposes of the Act`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlawful disclosure` MEANS 5000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for unlawful disclosure` MEANS 12
